"render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-descent-data}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:41698f8eabcfca91422ee10c3e33cd6d6f248433b56dd9f9061ef502162fdf81", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:30c5cc7313e99fa08cddb3b4c11146b55e69166984d312cbe9c06edf61f465b0", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a fibred category.\nMake a choice of pullbacks as in Categories,\nDefinition <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0003>\nbe a family of morphisms of <MATH_0004>. Assume all the fibre products\n<MATH_0005>, and <MATH_0006> exist.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>descent datum <MATH_0007> in <MATH_0008>\nrelative to the family <MATH_0009><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is given by an object <MATH_0010>\nof <MATH_0011> for each <MATH_0012>, an isomorphism\n<MATH_0013>\nin <MATH_0014> for each pair <MATH_0015>\nsuch that for every triple of indices <MATH_0016> the\ndiagram\n<MATH_0017>\nin the category <MATH_0018>\ncommutes. This is called the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>cocycle condition<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0003> A <TEXTITOPEN_0003>morphism <MATH_0019> of descent data<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> is given\nby a family <MATH_0020> of morphisms\n<MATH_0021> in <MATH_0022>\nsuch that all the diagrams\n<MATH_0023>\nin the categories <MATH_0024> commute.\n<STRUCT_0004> The category of descent data relative to\n<MATH_0025> is denoted <MATH_0026>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5e23fcd20c77fdb6e5831d3f35c5b0729b0dd78aaa2a0c55e13d818080ba042a", "unit_id": "tag:026B:statement"}
